<title>FRANCE: Sanofi prudent about acquisions.</title>
<headline>Sanofi prudent about acquisions.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>French health and beauty products company Sanofi has money to make acquisitons and plans to participate in a prudent way in the restructuring of the pharmaceuticals industry.</p>
<p>&quot;Indeed, we have the means for an acqusition,&quot; chairman Jean-Francois Dehecq told an analysts' briefing. &quot;But at the moment those acquisitions are very expensive and I am not sure that they are the best way to move forward because we have to get a return on these investments.</p>
<p>&quot;We will be very prudent about acquisitions.&quot;</p>
</text>
